<p>Israeli strikes in southern Lebanon on Tuesday killed eight people, including three Lebanese Civil Defence rescuers, Lebanon&#x27;s Health Ministry said. Lebanese authorities said successive strikes on a building in Majdal Zoun killed five people. Rescuers and Lebanese soldiers were working there after an initial attack; two Lebanese soldiers were wounded. Lebanon&#x27;s Civil Defence said three of its members had been trapped under rubble and were later found dead. The Israeli military did not immediately respond to requests for comment on the Majdal Zoun incident. The strikes occurred despite a ceasefire that took effect on April 17 and was later extended, according to reports citing President Trump. Israel has been fighting Hezbollah since early March, when it sent troops into southern Lebanon.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/Qm5WFQTDsiD26sjyGw8mSc5FLVUS7pSJiTiq16XtQKhZTYD0uQbdhzMlqaqBcbcUeXgX8_eMeJCDrUkeR-7DmtM1SyVblWSM8ci_Qx3bgR1KOxPlbU_Mw3sssHNAbRfRYhNJTgtd_MGnsUCX98N6YWRKEKWG00B5s95_OxtG0psKiVgUXFfWvUJKhDUQ2ngqBdQQBuhbeKaOU46ThUDSDUJPvDHUbCCvAmTdtF5ZvND9rlr6vJFGRrRgVaWAQTIBUx__BgaIkF2mClFjpw' alt='Explosions caused by the actions of Israeli troops in the southern Lebanese village of Arnoun on Tuesday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Wider toll: Lebanon&#x27;s Health Ministry said an Israeli attack on Zouaya killed one person and wounded 15 others, including five children.</li><li>Truce marker: Business Recorder reported that the army&#x27;s statement was the first time the Lebanese army had said Israeli strikes targeted its troops since the truce began.</li><li>Southern operations: Israel carried out heavy airstrikes and demolitions in southern Lebanon, including areas inside an Israeli-announced &quot;yellow line&quot; where residents had been warned not to return.</li><li>Previous-day toll: Lebanon&#x27;s Health Ministry said Israeli strikes on southern areas on Monday killed four people and injured 51.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>